  "$aliases": "Old item names merged into another item, read 1:1 from saves and the wire (`from` is no longer an item). The Rock was its own item, which the stone tools didn't take (owner, 2026-11-15: \"One item: rock = shard\"): dirt, grass and the ground's rocks give Rock shards, and saved Rocks load as Rock shards.",
  "aliases": [{ "from": "dwell:rock", "to": "dwell:rock_shard" }],
  "$wallets": "Currency items (with a `value`) go to the wallet, not a slot: a total up to its capacity (owner, 2026-11-08: the starting wallet holds 99; bigger wallets later).",
  "wallets": [{ "name": "dwell:pouch", "label": "Pouch", "capacity": 99 }],
  "$recipes": "Combining (owner, 2026-11-11): each recipe's `inputs` (items and counts, taken from anywhere in the inventory) make its `output`; applied by the server (InventoryAction::Combine, sent only to a server whose Inventory has inventory_flags::COMBINE), listed in the backpack's Combine section where items are used. `name` names it on the wire (unique); `label` (optional) names the Combine button, else the output item's label (a slab's item is its block, labelled \"Stone\": the recipe says \"Stone slab\"). A slab is a block's own item: the ½ m piece it places. The stone axe, the stone pickaxe and the stone shovel share their inputs (the player picks which); the wooden shovel is 4 sticks and 2 grass fibre (owner, 2026-11-14). Adventure starts with a wooden shovel (owner, 2026-11-14: \"Perhaps you could start with a wooden shovel instead of an axe since dirt drops rocks.\").",
